  "title": "Trimithis",
  "provenance": "Barrington Atlas: BAtlas 79 inset Trimithis?",
  "placeTypeURIs": [
    "https://pleiades.stoa.org/vocabularies/place-types/settlement",
    "https://pleiades.stoa.org/vocabularies/place-types/archaeological-site"
  ],
  "details": "<p>The site of Amheida, in Egypt's <a class=\"external-link\" href=\"../776172\">Dahkleh Oasis</a>, has been under active excavation since 2001 and is now led by a team from New York University. On that project's website (<a class=\"external-link\" href=\"http://www.amheida.org\">www.amheida.org</a>)<span>, one can find extensive and up-to-date information, including\u00a0<a href=\"http://amheida.org/index.php?content=publications\" target=\"_blank\">PDF copies of publications</a>,\u00a0<a href=\"http://amheida.org/index.php?content=reports\" target=\"_blank\">annual reports</a>,\u00a0<a href=\"http://amheida.org/index.php?content=maps\" target=\"_blank\">maps</a>\u00a0(including KML for download), and the\u00a0<a href=\"http://www.columbia.edu/cu/lweb/data/eresources/clio/DakhlehOasisLibraryCollection.htm\" target=\"_blank\">catalog of the dig house library</a>, as well as information about\u00a0<a href=\"http://amheida.org/index.php?content=student_info\" target=\"_blank\">NYU's undergraduate program in Egypt</a>\u00a0(an archaeological field school on-site</span>\u00a0at Amheida).</p>\r\n<p>The <a class=\"external-link\" href=\"http://www.nyu.edu/isaw/awib.htm\"><em>Ancient World Image Bank</em></a> (a publication of NYU's <a class=\"external-link\" href=\"http://www.nyu.edu/isaw/\">Institute for the Study of the Ancient World</a>, whose director runs the Amheida excavations) provides an <a class=\"external-link\" href=\"http://www.flickr.com/photos/isawnyu/sets/72157624340575014/\">extensive set of open-access imagery from the site</a>.</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "An ancient settlement of at least Roman and Late Antique date, situated in the Dahkleh Oasis at a site now called Amheida.",
